#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/at-the-grocery-store.ts:354
#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/returning-an-item-in-a-store.ts:22
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "Shopping"
msgstr "Shopping"

#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/at-the-grocery-store.ts:16
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Shopping at a grocery store involves many short but useful conversations. "
"You may need to find a product, ask about a price, understand a promotion, "
"check ingredients, or speak with a cashier.\n"
"\n"
"You do not need long or complicated sentences. Clear questions and polite "
"phrases are usually enough.\n"
"\n"
"## How to Ask Where Something Is\n"
"\n"
"When you cannot find a product, you can approach an employee and say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Excuse me, could you help me?”\n"
"- “Where can I find the milk?”\n"
"- “Which aisle is the pasta in?”\n"
"- “Do you know where the rice is?”\n"
"- “I’m looking for olive oil.”\n"
"- “Could you show me where it is?”\n"
"\n"
"An employee may respond with directions such as:\n"
"\n"
"- “It’s in aisle five.”\n"
"- “It’s next to the bread.”\n"
"- “You’ll find it at the back of the store.”\n"
"- “It’s on the top shelf.”\n"
"- “It’s in the refrigerated section.”\n"
"- “Follow me. I’ll show you.”\n"
"\n"
"Useful location words include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Aisle** — a passage between shelves\n"
"- **Shelf** — the surface where products are displayed\n"
"- **Checkout** — the place where you pay\n"
"- **Refrigerated section** — the area for chilled products\n"
"- **Frozen-food section** — the area containing frozen products\n"
"- **Produce section** — the area containing fruit and vegetables\n"
"- **Bakery section** — the area containing bread and baked goods\n"
"\n"
"## Ask Whether a Product Is Available\n"
"\n"
"Sometimes a shelf is empty or the product you need is difficult to find.\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you have this product?”\n"
"- “Do you sell oat milk?”\n"
"- “Is this item still available?”\n"
"- “Do you have any more in stock?”\n"
"- “When will this be available again?”\n"
"- “Is there another brand you would recommend?”\n"
"- “Do you have a similar product?”\n"
"\n"
"If the product is unavailable, an employee may say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m afraid it’s out of stock.”\n"
"- “We should have more tomorrow.”\n"
"- “That product has been discontinued.”\n"
"- “We have a similar one from another brand.”\n"
"- “Let me check in the storage room.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Prices\n"
"\n"
"Price labels can sometimes be unclear, especially when several products are "
"displayed together.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “How much is this?”\n"
"- “Could you check the price for me?”\n"
"- “Is this the correct price?”\n"
"- “Is the price per item or per kilogram?”\n"
"- “Does this include tax?”\n"
"- “Why is the price different at the checkout?”\n"
"- “Which one is cheaper?”\n"
"\n"
"You may also hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “It costs three ninety-nine.”\n"
"- “It’s sold by weight.”\n"
"- “The price is per kilogram.”\n"
"- “The discount is applied at the checkout.”\n"
"- “You need a loyalty card to get that price.”\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Promotions and Discounts\n"
"\n"
"Stores often use promotional language that may be confusing.\n"
"\n"
"Common offers include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Buy one, get one free**\n"
"- **Two for five**\n"
"- **Twenty percent off**\n"
"- **Reduced price**\n"
"- **Special offer**\n"
"- **Member price**\n"
"- **Loyalty-card price**\n"
"- **Clearance**\n"
"- **Valid until Friday**\n"
"\n"
"Questions you can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is this product on sale?”\n"
"- “How does this promotion work?”\n"
"- “Do I need to buy two?”\n"
"- “Do I need a loyalty card?”\n"
"- “Is the discount applied automatically?”\n"
"- “When does the promotion end?”\n"
"- “Can I combine this offer with another discount?”\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “The label says two for five. Can I buy only one?”\n"
"\n"
"The employee may explain:\n"
"\n"
"> “Yes, but one item will cost three.”\n"
"\n"
"## Compare Products\n"
"\n"
"You may want to compare brands, sizes, ingredients, or prices.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “What is the difference between these two?”\n"
"- “Which one is more popular?”\n"
"- “Which one is better value?”\n"
"- “Is there a cheaper option?”\n"
"- “Do you have a larger size?”\n"
"- “Does this come in a smaller package?”\n"
"- “Which brand would you recommend?”\n"
"- “Is there a store-brand version?”\n"
"\n"
"A useful phrase is:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’m looking for something similar, but less expensive.”\n"
"\n"
"You can also explain your priorities:\n"
"\n"
"- “I need something without added sugar.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for a high-protein option.”\n"
"- “I’d prefer something organic.”\n"
"- “I need a product that will last several days.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for the best value, not necessarily the cheapest product.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Ingredients and Dietary Needs\n"
"\n"
"Checking ingredients is especially important if you have allergies or "
"dietary preferences.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Does this contain nuts?”\n"
"- “Is this gluten-free?”\n"
"- “Is this suitable for vegetarians?”\n"
"- “Is this vegan?”\n"
"- “Does this contain dairy?”\n"
"- “Is there any added sugar?”\n"
"- “Where can I find lactose-free products?”\n"
"- “Do you have a dairy-free alternative?”\n"
"\n"
"You can also say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m allergic to peanuts.”\n"
"- “I cannot eat gluten.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for something without dairy.”\n"
"- “Could you help me check the ingredients?”\n"
"\n"
"For serious allergies, always read the package carefully. A store employee "
"may help you find information, but they may not be able to guarantee that a "
"product is completely allergen-free.\n"
"\n"
"## Buy Fruit, Vegetables, Meat, or Cheese\n"
"\n"
"Some products are sold by weight rather than by package.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’d like one kilogram of apples, please.”\n"
"- “Could I have half a kilogram of tomatoes?”\n"
"- “I’d like three hundred grams of cheese.”\n"
"- “Could you give me six slices?”\n"
"- “Can I have two chicken breasts?”\n"
"- “That’s enough, thank you.”\n"
"\n"
"The employee may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “How much would you like?”\n"
"- “Is this amount okay?”\n"
"- “Would you like it sliced?”\n"
"- “Would you like anything else?”\n"
"- “Do you need a bag?”\n"
"\n"
"You can respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “A little more, please.”\n"
"- “A little less, please.”\n"
"- “That amount is perfect.”\n"
"- “Could you slice it thinly?”\n"
"- “No, that’s everything.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Product Freshness\n"
"\n"
"You may want to check whether food is fresh or how long it will last.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “When does this expire?”\n"
"- “What is the use-by date?”\n"
"- “Was this baked today?”\n"
"- “Is this fresh?”\n"
"- “How long will this keep?”\n"
"- “Should I store this in the refrigerator?”\n"
"- “Can this be frozen?”\n"
"\n"
"Common date labels include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Best before** — the product may lose quality after this date\n"
"- **Use by** — the product should normally be consumed before this date\n"
"- **Packed on** — the date the product was packaged\n"
"- **Sell by** — a date mainly used by the store\n"
"\n"
"## Handle Problems with a Product\n"
"\n"
"You may notice that an item is damaged, open, expired, or incorrectly "
"labelled.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “This package is damaged.”\n"
"- “This bottle is leaking.”\n"
"- “I think this product has expired.”\n"
"- “The seal is broken.”\n"
"- “This item was on the wrong shelf.”\n"
"- “Could I exchange this for another one?”\n"
"- “Could someone check this product?”\n"
"\n"
"Stay polite and explain the problem clearly.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “Excuse me, this carton is leaking. Could I replace it?”\n"
"\n"
"## Speak at the Checkout\n"
"\n"
"When you reach the checkout, the cashier may ask several common questions:\n"
"\n"
"- “Did you find everything you needed?”\n"
"- “Do you have a loyalty card?”\n"
"- “Would you like a bag?”\n"
"- “Do you need a receipt?”\n"
"- “Are you paying by cash or card?”\n"
"- “Would you like to donate to charity?”\n"
"- “Do you need help packing?”\n"
"\n"
"Useful answers include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Yes, I found everything, thank you.”\n"
"- “No, I couldn’t find one item.”\n"
"- “I don’t have a loyalty card.”\n"
"- “Yes, one bag, please.”\n"
"- “No bag, thank you.”\n"
"- “I’ll pay by card.”\n"
"- “Could I have the receipt, please?”\n"
"- “Could I pay separately for these items?”\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Checkout Instructions\n"
"\n"
"When paying by card, you may hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “Please insert your card.”\n"
"- “You can tap your card.”\n"
"- “Please enter your PIN.”\n"
"- “Your payment was declined.”\n"
"- “Would you like to try again?”\n"
"- “Please remove your card.”\n"
"- “The payment has gone through.”\n"
"\n"
"If something goes wrong, you can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could I try another card?”\n"
"- “Can I pay in cash instead?”\n"
"- “I think I was charged twice.”\n"
"- “Could you check the total?”\n"
"- “The price on the shelf was different.”\n"
"- “Could you remove this item, please?”\n"
"\n"
"## Use Self-Checkout\n"
"\n"
"At a self-checkout, you may need to ask an employee for help.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you help me with the self-checkout?”\n"
"- “The machine is not scanning this item.”\n"
"- “It says there is an unexpected item.”\n"
"- “How do I weigh the vegetables?”\n"
"- “Where do I enter the product number?”\n"
"- “How can I remove an item?”\n"
"- “The machine has not printed my receipt.”\n"
"\n"
"You may see or hear instructions such as:\n"
"\n"
"- “Scan your first item.”\n"
"- “Place the item in the bagging area.”\n"
"- “Select your payment method.”\n"
"- “Approval needed.”\n"
"- “Please wait for assistance.”\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Grocery Store Conversation\n"
"\n"
"A typical interaction may look like this:\n"
"\n"
"> **Customer:** Excuse me, could you help me find oat milk?  \n"
"> **Employee:** Of course. It’s in aisle six, next to the regular milk.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Thank you. Do you have an unsweetened version?  \n"
"> **Employee:** Yes, we have two brands. This one is currently on sale.  \n"
"> **Customer:** How does the promotion work?  \n"
"> **Employee:** It’s twenty percent off if you have a loyalty card.  \n"
"> **Customer:** I don’t have one. Is there a cheaper alternative?  \n"
"> **Employee:** Yes, the store-brand version is less expensive.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Great. Could you show me where it is?\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Shopping Formula\n"
"\n"
"When you need help, use this structure:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Get attention:** “Excuse me, could you help me?”\n"
"2. **Explain what you need:** “I’m looking for brown rice.”\n"
"3. **Ask a specific question:** “Which aisle is it in?”\n"
"4. **Clarify the answer:** “Did you say aisle seven?”\n"
"5. **Thank the employee:** “Great, thank you for your help.”\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you are shopping at FreshMart. The AI employee will help "
"you find products, explain prices and promotions, and answer questions "
"about the store.\n"
"\n"
"During the conversation, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- Ask where at least one product is located.\n"
"- Ask about a price or promotion.\n"
"- Compare two products.\n"
"- Ask about an ingredient or dietary requirement.\n"
"- Respond to one small problem, such as an unavailable product or unclear "
"price.\n"
"- Complete the purchase or end the interaction politely.\n"
"\n"
"Focus on communicating your needs clearly. You do not need perfect grammar "
"to have a successful conversation in a grocery store."
msgstr ""
"Å handle i en dagligvarebutikk innebærer mange korte, men nyttige samtaler. "
"Du må kanskje finne et produkt, spørre om en pris, forstå en kampanje, "
"sjekke ingredienser, eller snakke med en kasserer.\n"
"\n"
"Du trenger ikke lange eller kompliserte setninger. Klare spørsmål og "
"høflige uttrykk er vanligvis nok.\n"
"\n"
"## Hvordan spørre hvor noe er\n"
"\n"
"Når du ikke kan finne et produkt, kan du henvende deg til en ansatt og si:\n"
"\n"
"- “Unnskyld, kan du hjelpe meg?”\n"
"- “Hvor kan jeg finne melken?”\n"
"- “Hvilken gang er pastaen i?”\n"
"- “Vet du hvor risen er?”\n"
"- “Jeg leter etter olivenolje.”\n"
"- “Kan du vise meg hvor det er?”\n"
"\n"
"En ansatt kan svare med veibeskrivelser som:\n"
"\n"
"- “Det er i gang fem.”\n"
"- “Det er ved siden av brødet.”\n"
"- “Du finner det bak i butikken.”\n"
"- “Det er på øverste hylle.”\n"
"- “Det er i den kjølte seksjonen.”\n"
"- “Følg meg. Jeg skal vise deg.”\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige lokasjonsord inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- **Gang** — en passasje mellom hyller\n"
"- **Hylle** — overflaten der produkter er utstilt\n"
"- **Kasse** — stedet hvor du betaler\n"
"- **Kjølt seksjon** — området for kjølte produkter\n"
"- **Fryseseksjon** — området som inneholder frosne produkter\n"
"- **Frukt- og grøntavdeling** — området som inneholder frukt og grønnsaker\n"
"- **Bakeriavdeling** — området som inneholder brød og bakverk\n"
"\n"
"## Spørre om et produkt er tilgjengelig\n"
"\n"
"Noen ganger er en hylle tom, eller produktet du trenger er vanskelig å "
"finne.\n"
"\n"
"Du kan spørre:\n"
"\n"
"- “Har dere dette produktet?”\n"
"- “Selger dere havremelk?”\n"
"- “Er denne varen fortsatt tilgjengelig?”\n"
"- “Har dere flere på lager?”\n"
"- “Når vil dette bli tilgjengelig igjen?”\n"
"- “Er det et annet merke du vil anbefale?”\n"
"- “Har dere et lignende produkt?”\n"
"\n"
"Hvis produktet ikke er tilgjengelig, kan en ansatt si:\n"
"\n"
"- “Jeg beklager, det er utsolgt.”\n"
"- “Vi burde få flere i morgen.”\n"
"- “Det produktet er avviklet.”\n"
"- “Vi har en lignende fra et annet merke.”\n"
"- “La meg sjekke på lageret.”\n"
"\n"
"## Spørre om priser\n"
"\n"
"Prisetiketter kan noen ganger være uklare, spesielt når flere produkter er "
"utstilt sammen.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige spørsmål inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- “Hvor mye koster dette?”\n"
"- “Kan du sjekke prisen for meg?”\n"
"- “Er dette riktig pris?”\n"
"- “Er prisen per vare eller per kilo?”\n"
"- “Inkluderer dette moms?”\n"
"- “Hvorfor er prisen forskjellig ved kassen?”\n"
"- “Hvilken er billigere?”\n"
"\n"
"Du kan også høre:\n"
"\n"
"- “Det koster tre nittini.”\n"
"- “Det er solgt etter vekt.”\n"
"- “Prisen er per kilo.”\n"
"- “Rabatten blir brukt i kassen.”\n"
"- “Du trenger et bonuskort for å få den prisen.”\n"
"\n"
"## Forstå kampanjer og rabatter\n"
"\n"
"Butikker bruker ofte kampanjespråk som kan være forvirrende.\n"
"\n"
"Vanlige tilbud inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- **Kjøp en, få en gratis**\n"
"- **To for fem**\n"
"- **Tjue prosent avslag**\n"
"- **Redusert pris**\n"
"- **Spesialtilbud**\n"
"- **Medlemspris**\n"
"- **Bonuskort-pris**\n"
"- **Ryddesalg**\n"
"- **Gyldig til fredag**\n"
"\n"
"Spørsmål du kan stille:\n"
"\n"
"- “Er dette produktet på salg?”\n"
"- “Hvordan fungerer denne kampanjen?”\n"
"- “Trenger jeg å kjøpe to?”\n"
"- “Trenger jeg et bonuskort?”\n"
"- “Blir rabatten brukt automatisk?”\n"
"- “Når slutter kampanjen?”\n"
"- “Kan jeg kombinere dette tilbudet med en annen rabatt?”\n"
"\n"
"For eksempel:\n"
"\n"
"> “Etiketten sier to for fem. Kan jeg kjøpe bare en?”\n"
"\n"
"Den ansatte kan forklare:\n"
"\n"
"> “Ja, men en vare vil koste tre.”\n"
"\n"
"## Sammenligne produkter\n"
"\n"
"Du vil kanskje sammenligne merker, størrelser, ingredienser eller priser.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige spørsmål inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- “Hva er forskjellen mellom disse to?”\n"
"- “Hvilken er mer populær?”\n"
"- “Hvilken gir bedre verdi?”\n"
"- “Finnes det et billigere alternativ?”\n"
"- “Har dere en større størrelse?”\n"
"- “Kommer dette i en mindre pakke?”\n"
"- “Hvilket merke vil du anbefale?”\n"
"- “Finnes det en butikkmerke-versjon?”\n"
"\n"
"Et nyttig uttrykk er:\n"
"\n"
"> “Jeg leter etter noe lignende, men rimeligere.”\n"
"\n"
"Du kan også forklare dine prioriteringer:\n"
"\n"
"- “Jeg trenger noe uten tilsatt sukker.”\n"
"- “Jeg leter etter et høyprotein-alternativ.”\n"
"- “Jeg ville foretrekke noe økologisk.”\n"
"- “Jeg trenger et produkt som varer flere dager.”\n"
"- “Jeg leter etter mest verdi, ikke nødvendigvis det billigste produktet.”\n"
"\n"
"## Spørre om ingredienser og kostholdspreferanser\n"
"\n"
"Å sjekke ingredienser er spesielt viktig hvis du har allergier eller "
"kostholdspreferanser.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige spørsmål inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- “Inneholder dette nøtter?”\n"
"- “Er dette glutenfritt?”\n"
"- “Er dette egnet for vegetarianere?”\n"
"- “Er dette vegansk?”\n"
"- “Inneholder dette meieriprodukter?”\n"
"- “Er det noe tilsatt sukker?”\n"
"- “Hvor kan jeg finne laktosefrie produkter?”\n"
"- “Har dere et melkefritt alternativ?”\n"
"\n"
"Du kan også si:\n"
"\n"
"- “Jeg er allergisk mot peanøtter.”\n"
"- “Jeg kan ikke spise gluten.”\n"
"- “Jeg leter etter noe uten meieriprodukter.”\n"
"- “Kan du hjelpe meg å sjekke ingrediensene?”\n"
"\n"
"For alvorlige allergier, les alltid pakken nøye. En butikkansatt kan hjelpe "
"deg med å finne informasjon, men de kan ikke garantere at et produkt er "
"helt uten allergener.\n"
"\n"
"## Kjøpe frukt, grønnsaker, kjøtt eller ost\n"
"\n"
"Noen produkter selges etter vekt i stedet for pakke.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige uttrykk inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- “Jeg vil gjerne ha ett kilo epler, takk.”\n"
"- “Kan jeg få en halv kilo tomater?”\n"
"- “Jeg vil gjerne ha tre hundre gram ost.”\n"
"- “Kan du gi meg seks skiver?”\n"
"- “Kan jeg få to kyllingbryst?”\n"
"- “Det er nok, takk.”\n"
"\n"
"Den ansatte kan spørre:\n"
"\n"
"- “Hvor mye vil du ha?”\n"
"- “Er denne mengden ok?”\n"
"- “Vil du ha det i skiver?”\n"
"- “Vil du ha noe annet?”\n"
"- “Trenger du en pose?”\n"
"\n"
"Du kan svare:\n"
"\n"
"- “Litt mer, vær så snill.”\n"
"- “Litt mindre, takk.”\n"
"- “Den mengden er perfekt.”\n"
"- “Kan du skjære det tynt?”\n"
"- “Nei, det er alt.”\n"
"\n"
"## Spørre om produktets friskhet\n"
"\n"
"Du vil kanskje sjekke om maten er fersk eller hvor lenge den vil vare.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige spørsmål inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- “Når går dette ut?”\n"
"- “Hva er siste forbruksdato?”\n"
"- “Ble dette bakt i dag?”\n"
"- “Er dette ferskt?”\n"
"- “Hvor lenge vil dette holde?”\n"
"- “Bør jeg oppbevare dette i kjøleskapet?”\n"
"- “Kan dette fryses?”\n"
"\n"
"Vanlige datomerkinger inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- **Best før** — produktet kan miste kvalitet etter denne datoen\n"
"- **Brukes innen** — produktet bør normalt brukes før denne datoen\n"
"- **Pakket på** — datoen produktet ble pakket\n"
"- **Selges innen** — en dato som hovedsakelig brukes av butikken\n"
"\n"
"## Håndtere problemer med et produkt\n"
"\n"
"Du kan legge merke til at en vare er skadet, åpen, utgått på dato, eller "
"feilmerket.\n"
"\n"
"Du kan si:\n"
"\n"
"- “Denne pakken er skadet.”\n"
"- “Denne flasken lekker.”\n"
"- “Jeg tror dette produktet har gått ut på dato.”\n"
"- “Forseglingen er brutt.”\n"
"- “Denne varen var på feil hylle.”\n"
"- “Kan jeg bytte denne til en annen?”\n"
"- “Kan noen sjekke dette produktet?”\n"
"\n"
"Vær høflig og forklare problemet tydelig.\n"
"\n"
"For eksempel:\n"
"\n"
"> “Unnskyld meg, denne kartongen lekker. Kan jeg bytte den?”\n"
"\n"
"## Snakke ved kassen\n"
"\n"
"Når du kommer til kassen, kan kassereren stille flere vanlige spørsmål:\n"
"\n"
"- “Fant du alt du trengte?”\n"
"- “Har du et bonuskort?”\n"
"- “Vil du ha en pose?”\n"
"- “Trenger du en kvittering?”\n"
"- “Betaler du med kontanter eller kort?”\n"
"- “Vil du gi til veldedighet?”\n"
"- “Trenger du hjelp med å pakke?”\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige svar inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- “Ja, jeg fant alt, takk.”\n"
"- “Nei, jeg fant ikke én vare.”\n"
"- “Jeg har ikke et bonuskort.”\n"
"- “Ja, en pose, takk.”\n"
"- “Ingen pose, takk.”\n"
"- “Jeg betaler med kort.”\n"
"- “Kan jeg få kvitteringen, takk?”\n"
"- “Kan jeg betale separat for disse varene?”\n"
"\n"
"## Forstå instruksjoner ved kassen\n"
"\n"
"Når du betaler med kort, kan du høre:\n"
"\n"
"- “Vennligst sett inn kortet ditt.”\n"
"- “Du kan tappe kortet ditt.”\n"
"- “Vennligst tast inn PIN-koden din.”\n"
"- “Betalingen ble avvist.”\n"
"- “Vil du prøve igjen?”\n"
"- “Vennligst ta ut kortet ditt.”\n"
"- “Betalingen har gått igjennom.”\n"
"\n"
"Hvis noe går galt, kan du si:\n"
"\n"
"- “Kan jeg prøve et annet kort?”\n"
"- “Kan jeg betale kontant i stedet?”\n"
"- “Jeg tror jeg ble belastet to ganger.”\n"
"- “Kan du sjekke totalen?”\n"
"- “Prisen på hyllen var annerledes.”\n"
"- “Kan du fjerne denne varen, vær så snill?”\n"
"\n"
"## Bruke selvbetjent kasse\n"
"\n"
"Ved en selvbetjent kasse kan det være nødvendig å be en ansatt om hjelp.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige uttrykk inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- “Kan du hjelpe meg med selvbetjeningskassen?”\n"
"- “Maskinen skanner ikke denne varen.”\n"
"- “Det står at det er en uventet gjenstand.”\n"
"- “Hvordan veier jeg grønnsakene?”\n"
"- “Hvor skriver jeg inn produktnummeret?”\n"
"- “Hvordan kan jeg fjerne en vare?”\n"
"- “Maskinen har ikke skrevet ut kvitteringen min.”\n"
"\n"
"Du kan se eller høre instruksjoner som:\n"
"\n"
"- “Skann den første varen din.”\n"
"- “Plasser varen i poseområdet.”\n"
"- “Velg betalingsmetoden din.”\n"
"- “Godkjenning nødvendig.”\n"
"- “Vennligst vent på assistanse.”\n"
"\n"
"## En enkel dagligvarebutikk samtale\n"
"\n"
"En typisk interaksjon kan se slik ut:\n"
"\n"
"> **Kunde:** Unnskyld, kan du hjelpe meg å finne havremelk?  \n"
"> **Ansatt:** Selvfølgelig. Det er i gang seks, ved siden av vanlig melk.  \n"
"> **Kunde:** Takk. Har dere en usøtet versjon?  \n"
"> **Ansatt:** Ja, vi har to merker. Denne er for tiden på salg.  \n"
"> **Kunde:** Hvordan fungerer kampanjen?  \n"
"> **Ansatt:** Det er tjue prosent avslag hvis du har et bonuskort.  \n"
"> **Kunde:** Jeg har ikke ett. Finnes det et billigere alternativ?  \n"
"> **Ansatt:** Ja, butikkmerket er rimeligere.  \n"
"> **Kunde:** Flott. Kan du vise meg hvor det er?\n"
"\n"
"## En enkel handleformel\n"
"\n"
"Når du trenger hjelp, bruk denne strukturen:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Få oppmerksomhet:** “Unnskyld, kan du hjelpe meg?”\n"
"2. **Forklar hva du trenger:** “Jeg leter etter brun ris.”\n"
"3. **Still et spesifikt spørsmål:** “Hvilken gang er det i?”\n"
"4. **Klargjøre svaret:** “Sa du gang syv?”\n"
"5. **Takk den ansatte:** “Flott, takk for hjelpen.”\n"
"\n"
"## Øvelsesscenario\n"
"\n"
"I denne rollespillet handler du på FreshMart. Den AI-baserte ansatte vil "
"hjelpe deg med å finne produkter, forklare priser og kampanjer, og svare på "
"spørsmål om butikken.\n"
"\n"
"Under samtalen, prøv å:\n"
"\n"
"- Spørre hvor minst ett produkt er lokalisert.\n"
"- Spørre om en pris eller kampanje.\n"
"- Sammenligne to produkter.\n"
"- Spørre om en ingrediens eller kostholdskrav.\n"
"- Svar på ett lite problem, som et utilgjengelig produkt eller en uklar "
"pris.\n"
"- Fullføre kjøpet eller avslutte interaksjonen høflig.\n"
"\n"
"Fokuser på å formidle dine behov tydelig. Du trenger ikke perfekt "
"grammatikk for å ha en vellykket samtale i en dagligvarebutikk."

